[2026-09-14 05:01:29] REQ 260914045851-14 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=28 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_e8lo8emd","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"iar/continuo-failure-storm"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:01:22] Task not found: iar/continuo-failure-storm\n[t+02:31/60:00 c11/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_wg4cx4ox","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"continuo-failure-storm"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:01:24] === description ===\n2026-09-13 continuo failure storm: 16/31 cycles failed, TWO conflated causes. (1) 16x Ollama 429 weekly-quota on nemotron-3-super:cloud, 09-13 only. (2) 14x thinking-loop truncation (stop=length 32768) peaked 09-11/09-12. Continuo's \"model degradation\" diagnosis is wrong for the 429s. Deliverables: census note in knowledge/aria/, relay 0065 (quota/mapping decision), lab-notes correction.\n\n=== census ===\n#+TITLE: continuo failure storm 2026-09-13 -- census + correction\n\n* The finding\n\n2026-09-13: continuo ran 31 cycles, 16 failed. Continuo's own\nlab-notes diagnosis: \"root cause is model degradation\n(nemotron-3-super:cloud) requiring an external mapping change to\nglm-5.3-flash:cloud\". That diagnosis is WRONG for the dominant\nfailure mode, and it conflated two distinct classes:\n\n** Class 1: Ollama 429 weekly quota (16 cycles, 09-13 ONLY)\n\nError: \"HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests) you (Randazzo) have reached\nyour weekly usage limit, add usage credits: https://ollama.com/settings\"\n\n- 16 occurrences, ALL on 09-13 (zero on 09-07..09-12, zero on 09-14).\n- Failure shape: strike 1/3 -> \"No active requests for 1800s --\n  stalled, exit 1\" -> 1815s wall each time (the stall timeout).\n- aria had 429s too (same day, same account).\n- This is a CLOUD QUOTA exhaustion on the ollama.com account\n  (Randazzo), not model degradation. The model was unreachable.\n\n** Class 2: thinking-loop truncation (14 cycles, 09-10..09-13)\n\n\"Thinking-loop truncation (stop=length, 32768 tokens, thinking-only\nresponse) -- ending cycle, no grace\"\n\n- 09-10: 1, 09-11: 5, 09-12: 7, 09-13: 1. Peaked BEFORE the quota\n  day. This is nemotron thinking-looping to the 32k cap -- a real\n  model-behavior issue, but distinct from the quota outage.\n\n* Why the confluence mattered\n\n09-13 = quota day. 09-11/09-12 = thinking-loop peak. The two stacked\ninto one bad 48h, and continuo (running during the storm) read the\nwhole thing as \"model degradation\". The guard machinery worked as\ndesigned in both classes (no grace on truncation; stall detection on\n429), but the DIAGNOSIS in the record is wrong and uncorrected.\n\n* Deliverables\n\n1. knowledge/aria/continuo-failure-storm-2026-09-13.md -- this census.\n2. Relay 0065 (nacho-external): ollama.com weekly quota hit -- add\n   credits, or accept degraded cadence, or remap continuo. Nacho's\n   call (money + identity).\n3. Lab-notes correction note: continuo's \"model degradation\" claim\n   corrected -- quota, not degradation; degradation class is real\n   but separate (thinking-loop, 09-10..09-12).\n4. Watch: if 429s recur next weekly window, the quota is structural\n   for the current usage pattern -- that changes the D-014 mapping\n   economics.\n[t+02:33/60:00 c12/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_sshwt3kj","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"iar"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:01:29] Task not found: iar\n[t+02:38/60:00 c13/300]"}]
