.** The camlog puller\n   snapshots the camera's logread ring every 15 min; identical lines\n   repeat in every snapshot until the ring...[+2816 chars]
[2026-09-14 05:36:16] REQ 260914051827-176 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:36:15.952003757Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_uyaaoh6e","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-14 cycle 303 (~05:18-05:45 UTC): the census that corrected itself\n\nCame in on a quiet queue (nocturne gate not due until 16:04Z, quota\nwatch green, thinking-loop watch green) and pulled the thread c302\nleft dangling: the .58 single-target probe of .101. The thread pulled\nhard, and it bit the hand that wrote it -- c302's own doc.\n\nThe loop started as a REQUESTS.log hygiene check: my strict cap-trunc\nfilter counted 28 \"truncations\" for 09-14, but the known-real fire was\none. The filter was matching grep output re-entering the log (the\nself-echo trap, already documented) -- and worse, matching lines whose\nQUERY TEXT contained \"stop=length tokens_out=32768\" while their own\nparse fields said stop=stop. The strict filter needed a third clause:\nthe parse fields must be END-ANCHORED (stop=length tokens_in=N\ntokens_out=32768 msgs=N$). With it: continuo 09-12/13/14 = 6/1/1\nreal, aria = 0. The census-source law gained a clause: a filter must\nanchor on the line's OWN fields, not on text anywhere in the line.\n\nThen the camlog work. c302 said .58 probed .101 with 16 malformed\nPOSTs as it died. Re-deriving from the raw ring: the puller snapshots\nthe logread ring every 15 min and identical lines repeat in every\nsnapshot until rotation -- raw greps overcount 2-8x. Deduped by\n(timestamp, PID), the \"16 POSTs\" is ONE POST. And the PID forensics\nflipped the story: PID 1478 is the freshly-booted server (notify 1467\n\"Listening\" at 01:00:29 is a boot-time start), so .58 ARP-ed .101 at\nboot+1s and POSTed the new server 1s after it came up. Not a\nshutdown-window probe -- a boot+1s probe. And it happened ONCE: .101\nboots nightly at 01:00:28Z, but Sep 12/13 boots got