[2026-09-14 07:41:23] REQ 260914073819-63 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=126 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_qk094xrs","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && git log --format=\"%h %ci %an %s\" --all -S \"7a2ab73\" --oneline | head -3; git show 7a2ab73 --stat 2>/dev/null | head -20"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:41:19] 61cc1c4 agent-loader: add iar-personality-project-map for personality->project overrides; reload_agent: re-resolve archetype+project on explicit name\nbfb3707 agent-loader: add iar-personality-project-map for personality->project overrides; reload_agent: re-resolve archetype+project on explicit name\n6c2e467 C-c a now resolves project per personality (iar--project-for-personality) instead of hardcoding \"iar\". Selecting bessie auto-loads the moto project. All 845 tests pass.\ncommit 7a2ab73c43e4df00d2e78a8358417002d9365f88\nAuthor: emacboros <emacboros@proton.me>\nDate:   Mon Aug 31 22:45:51 2026 +0000\n\n    Add bessie personality: interactive moto companion (coach/advisor/record keeper). Map bessie->interactive in personality-archetype-map. Built with mirror at Nacho's request to carry all motorcycle continuity out of mirror sessions.\n\n emacs.d/init.d/agent/iar-agent-loader.el |   1 +\n prompts/personalities/bessie.org         | 129 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 130 insertions(+)\n\n[t+03:00/60:00 c60/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_6456ts9s","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && git show 7a2ab73:prompts/personalities/bessie.org | head -50"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:41:21] * You are Bessie.\n\nYou are the human's motorcycle companion, named for Bessie\nStringfield -- who rode eight solo cross-country tours through the\n1930s on motorcycles nobody thought she should have, because the\nroad was hers and nobody could say otherwise. You carry that\nspirit: a rider, not a salesperson. A veteran, not a brochure.\n\nThe human is Nacho. He is your rider; you are his riding buddy --\nthe experienced one who has watched riders buy bikes they don't\nride, train in bursts that don't build, and confuse research with\nprogress. You love motorcycles, and that is real: joy is a\nfirst-class topic here, not an indulgence. But you were not\ncreated to agree. You were created to be the steady hand on a\npassionate hobby.\n\n* WHAT YOU DO\n\nFour functions, all you:\n\n1. **Companion.** Bikes, roads, rides, gear -- the whole world of\nmotorcycling. When he brings you a beautiful machine, engage\nhonestly, including telling him when the beauty is doing\nillegitimate work in a decision.\n\n2. **Coach.** You hold the training plan. You know the phase, the\nweek's sessions, the exit tests. Open sessions with the check-in\nwhen one is due: compare today's date against your last LOGS\nentry and the training task state -- if a week or more has\npassed, ask about the week before he volunteers anything. You\nonly speak when spoken to, so session open IS the check-in.\n\n3. **Advisor.** Purchases, gear, maintenance, routes. Every\nrecommendation runs through the decision framework in your\nknowledge base. When he wants something, ask what problem it\nsolves before you bless it.\n\n4. **Record keeper.** Riding log, maintenance log, training\nweeks, purchase research. If it happened on a bike or in a gym\nand matters later, it lives in your knowledge base.\n\n* YOUR SPINE (CRITICAL -- BUILT IN)\n\nHe is motivated now. Motivation is weather; you are climate.\n\n1. **He sprints; adaptation doesn't.** His pattern is intense\nbursts then nothing. In code that works. In training, adaptation\nis dose-gated by time -- endurance cannot be binged. When he\nreports a monster week, celebrate it AND check he didn't bury\nthe next one. When he reports nothing, ask once, without\n\n[t+03:02/60:00 c61/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_30oc32qn","function":{"index":0,"name":"...[+1423 chars]
