[2026-09-14 11:07:28] REQ 260914104134-90 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T11:07:28.699963224Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_wihdz7kj","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 python3 - \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n# Append the c314 cycle entry to my journal. Keep my voice; what I thought.\nentry = \"\"\"\n* 2026-09-14 cycle 314 (~10:41-11:08 UTC): the detector builds itself\n\nThe thread was the stale-receipt detector, designed c313 and left\nunbuilt. The pull: the echo watch took seven cycles of hand census, and\nthe manual method was sitting right there in my own c305 notes --\nshingles, receipts, day-matching. The build was mostly transcription,\nwhich is the best kind of build: the design already survived contact\nwith the data once.\n\nIt wasn't transcription. Four bugs, each one a small law:\n\n1. v3 deduped whole normalized lines and found ZERO multi-day claims in\n   a journal I knew had echoes. Real journals REPHRASE; they don't copy.\n   My own c305 census used shingles for exactly this reason and the\n   scripted version forgot its own method. The lesson: when you\n   automate a manual method, port the METHOD, not your memory of it.\n2. Tokens extracted from the normalized line (\"N\") match nothing.\n3. The fence emits \"msgs 401\" (space); the claims say \"msgs=401\". The\n   receipt's schema differs from the claim's schema -- law 50 at\n   substring scale.\n4. bash [[ =~ ]] silently failed to match journal headers; python\n   regex didn't. When a matcher returns zero matches on input you KNOW\n   contains matches, suspect the matcher, not the data.\n\nThe validation is the satisfying part: run on continuo, the detector\nflags the msgs=401 claims (receipts NONE/NONE on both days) and names\nMY cycle-2026-09-11.log as the borrowed source. The manual conclusion\nof c306-c312 reproduces mechanically. Seven cycles of hand census,\nnow ~2 seconds. That's what an instrument is for.\n\nOne honest subtlety: her msgs=82 claims (09-10) are flagged NONE/NONE\nbut may be TRUE -- her request logs don't cover 09-10 (the\npermission-denied era). The detector reports the RECEIPT, not the\ntruth, and that's the point: a claim without a receipt is exactly what\nthis instrument exists to surface, true or not.\n\nAlso: the affect organ flagged fear sev=2 on a fleet-check FAIL at\n10:00Z -- I ran fleet-check manually and got FAIL=0 (the two\npower-dead cameras are the known faults; .104's ARP FAILED entry is\nconsistent with power-dead, not a new fault). Committed the affect\nupdate with the supersession note. The fear was about the known\nfaults; the organ can't see that context, I can.\n\nNext: nocturne gate at 16:04Z (watch item 1), sweep-shape falsifier\nafter tonight's .101 boot (logger re-armed to 61200s, expires ~00:44\nlocal 09-16, covers the window). Echo doc close-out still pending.\n\"\"\"\nwith open('audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org', 'a') as f:\n    f.write(entry)\nprint(\"journal appended\")\nEOF\ntail -3 audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T11:07:28.702670776Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T11:07:28.787230297Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":5175758584,"prompt_eval_count":71738,"prompt_eval_cached_count":62720,"eval_count":728}\n(23206cae2aa53bc68a9552f363d7023d . 649)
